{"type":"text","timestamp":1778441984190,"sessionID":"ses_1ec98f55affedMDP43pzdTDI9q","part":{"id":"prt_e136712e60015jt2KZ94D4vclc","messageID":"msg_e13670af4001VXbfqNd9Au3N8B","sessionID":"ses_1ec98f55affedMDP43pzdTDI9q","type":"text","text":"I'll work on this proof. The key insight is that if `u` tends to `l`, then `u ∘ φ` also tends to `l` for any strictly monotone `φ`, since `φ` tends to infinity.","time":{"start":1778441982694,"end":1778441984189}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778441988416,"sessionID":"ses_1ec98f55affedMDP43pzdTDI9q","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"lean-checker_check_lean_proof","callID":"toolu_01K3j6AY5y2whM3r3QJMZaUV","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"code":"import Mathlib\n\ntheorem subsequence_has_same_limit\n    {α : Type*} [TopologicalSpace α] {u : ℕ → α} {l : α}\n    (hu : Filter.Tendsto u Filter.atTop (nhds l)) :\n    ∀ φ : ℕ → ℕ, StrictMono φ →\n      ∃ m : α, Filter.Tendsto (fun n => u (φ n)) Filter.atTop (nhds m) ∧ m = l := by\n  intro φ hφ\n  refine ⟨l, ?_, rfl⟩\n  exact hu.comp hφ.tendsto_atTop\n"},"output":"{\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"calls_used\": 1,\n  \"calls_budget\": 10,\n  \"diagnostics\": []\n}","metadata":{"truncated":false},"title":"","time":{"start":1778441985999,"end":1778441988415},"attachments":[]},"metadata":{"anthropic":{"caller":{"type":"direct"}}},"id":"prt_e136718be002Af3NfJjcGj16se","sessionID":"ses_1ec98f55affedMDP43pzdTDI9q","messageID":"msg_e13670af4001VXbfqNd9Au3N8B"}}
